{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"situation awareness situation awareness","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md","fileName":"Situation Awareness.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Situation Awareness","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human Cognition]] [[Augmented Reality Navigation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Augmented Reality Navigation","Decision-Making","Navigation","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"situation awareness situation awareness","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md","fileName":"Situation Awareness.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Situation Awareness","heading":"Situation Awareness","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Situation awareness is an internal model of the current state of a user's environment. It includes perceiving relevant elements across time and space, understanding their meaning, and projecting how their status may change in the near future.\n\nThe model can include spatial relationships, other users, and task states, making it a basis for [[Decision-Making]]. In [[Navigation]], situation awareness depends on both spatial orientation—knowing one's location and viewing direction—and [[Spatial Knowledge]] stored in a [[Cognitive Map]].\n\nA 3D interface can support situation awareness with overviews, landmarks, maps, and clearly managed viewpoint changes.\n\nMobile AR can add registered information about relevant objects while allowing the user to continue looking at the physical surroundings. This can improve discovery and awareness, but excessive or poorly placed augmentation can also cover the evidence the user needs to perceive the situation directly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Augmented Reality Navigation","Decision-Making","Navigation","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"situation awareness situation awareness","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Situation Awareness.md","fileName":"Situation Awareness.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Situation Awareness","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Augmented Reality Navigation","Decision-Making","Navigation","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}